-- **Services and controllers**: Server features are Knit services (`Knit.CreateService { Name = ..., Client = { ... } }`) under `src/server/Modules/`; client features are Knit controllers (`Knit.CreateController`) under `src/client/Modules/`. `Knit.AddServicesDeep` / `AddControllersDeep` `require` every ModuleScript under those folders (helpers included), so a new service or controller needs no registry edit, and every helper placed there is loaded at startup and must be safe to require early. A helper under `src/client/Modules/` must return a table because `init.client.luau` indexes each result. A service that needs another resolves it with `Knit.GetService("Name")` at call time, not at require time.
